  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Request and streaming",
      "items": [
        "WebUI, console, Android app and CLI speak the same API on :8790 with a Bearer token (plus HTTPS on :8791 for a secure context).",
        "The client can steer/abort a live run (POST /api/chat/steer, /api/agent/control).",
        "Response: agentloop -> gateway -> client (SSE). The event feed is a second SSE channel.",
        "Every turn persists a user message + a response (or an explicit error turn)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Agentic loop and test-time control",
      "items": [
        "Prompt Assembly: the prompt is NOT just the user message — it is self-summary + tool registry + rules + skills + memory + state todo.",
        "The harness INJECTS synthetic messages into the LLM (nudge, observations, 'continue', steer) via _inject: the model sees them, and they appear in chat as harness.inject.",
        "control -> router: best-of-N calls the router N times and picks the best (prm.rank_text). N grows with difficulty.",
        "keepgoing: if open steps remain it REFUNDS the budget and re-injects the list; it never abandons a plan.",
        "verifier: apply-only-if-green — a red sandbox check means the edit is rolled back.",
        "subagent: child runs with a depth cap."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Security: registry, hooks, sandbox",
      "items": [
        "registry.py loads config/tools.yaml + overlay: a declarative allowlist (auto | required | denied | disabled).",
        "Approval gate: read-only auto, world-touching required, destructive deny.",
        "Hooks gate: deterministic scripts, no model. PreToolUse exit 2 BLOCKS the tool; PostToolUse receives the observation; Stop closes the turn.",
        "Sandbox: docker / bwrap / nsjail, --network none, read-only rootfs; fallback host 'none'.",
        "Tool Executor runs with cwd = session folder (workspace), not the sandbox scratch."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "State, self-improvement, extensibility",
      "items": [
        "Harness state: sessions, graph, append-only memory. It is WRITTEN and RE-READ every turn.",
        "Memory and the task graph are AUTO-INJECTED into the prompt (read context).",
        "Self-evolution: selfevolve mines sequences -> drafts a skill -> verifies in sandbox -> promotes only if the HELD-OUT gate is green (fail-closed), then archives. improve: memory=auto, skill/project/global=propose, code=forbidden.",
        "heldout.py: a SEALED judge suite outside the workspace (hash manifest, ~/.longrun/heldout). The agent cannot read or tamper with it; LONGRUN_REQUIRE_HELDOUT=0 disables it.",
        "Bidirectional MCP: external tools enter the registry (mcp -> registry); the harness IS an MCP server, an external client drives it (mcp -> gateway).",
        "Observability: metrics/OTel do NOT enter the LLM. Feed and traces return to the client."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Agents (AX), Jobs (JN) and the Control deck",
      "items": [
        "Every session can be designated an AGENT (AX): name, role (ROLE.md via roles.py) and reports_to (org chart). Storage data/agents.json.",
        "A JOB (JN) orchestrates several agents: goal, mode coordinator|fanout, deps (DAG) and blocked_by; independent waves run in parallel, the next waits. Storage data/jobs.json.",
        "Dispatch reuses the same turn machinery (server.chat_stream_gen): every agent turn is a real, persisted turn with its own task list.",
        "HTTP surface in orchestration.py (routed by api_v02.handle): /api/agents, /api/agents/tree, /api/jobs, /api/jobs/<id>/dispatch, /api/jobs/wake, /api/roles.",
        "The Control deck (orbit/) dispatches goals to one or more sessions in the background (Orchestrator.dispatch) and shows the job constellation.",
        "Knowledge/index: a per-workspace FTS+vector index (codeindex.py) and a global notebook index (knowledge.py) feed chunks into prompt assembly; both are built lazily and re-embeddable.",
        "JAG-350: the read-only `sessions` tool inside the Tool Executor — `list` maps sessions -> agent names, `read` returns the full transcript (messages + tool calls + injections). A coordinator can inspect a failing teammate and help it. The delegation record carries each teammate's sid."
      ]
    }
  ]
